        "problem": "Given that $\u2016u+5v\u2016=19$ and $\u2016u\u2016=4$, find the smallest possible value of $\u2016v\u2016.$",
        "worked_solution": "Using the triangle inequality, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2016u+5v\u2016 & \\le \u2016u\u2016+\u20165v\u2016.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2016u+5v\u2016 & \\le \u2016u\u2016+5\u2016v\u2016 \\\\ 19 & \\le 4+5\u2016v\u2016 \\\\ 15 & \\le 5\u2016v\u2016 \\\\ 3 & \\le \u2016v\u2016.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $\u2016v\u2016$ is $3.$",
